BAR Droid phone version of BAR's Context Build (luaui/widgets/cmd_context_build.lua): a building's sea twin (Solar ->
Tidal Generator, Bot Lab -> Shipyard, Sentry -> Harpoon, ...) armed only by where the pointer really points. BAR's
widget swaps the picked building for its twin whenever the ground under the pointer is at the water's level, every frame
while one is picked. On a phone the pointer stays where the last tap left it: often the void past the map's edge,
which traces to the water's plane, or water tapped for something else, so the dock's Bot Lab armed a Shipyard ghost
until the building's spot was tapped (the night's touch playtest, 2026-11-22, docs/PLAYTEST.md "sea twin"). Here:
- no swap with the pointer on the app's dock or BAR's interface (bardroid_portrait.lua's onDock, bardroid_touch.lua's
  WG.BarDroidOnInterface), nor past the map's edge (no building stands there);
- with fingers (not the pad: WG.BarDroidPadOnly), a building just picked stays the one picked until the pointer moves:
  a map tap ("spot": bardroid_touch.lua warps the pointer there) or the build menu copy keeping the pointer on the
  waiting building after a pan; each move is tested once, where the pointer then is. The pad's pointer stays in the
  middle while the camera moves under it: BAR's every-frame test there, as on a PC.
Applied by the engine (BarDroidPhoneLuaDir) to BAR's file as LuaUI loads it; if a block finds no place, BAR's own file
runs.

@@@ find
-- DrawWorld because update doesn't run pregame
function widget:DrawWorld()
@@@ with
-- BAR Droid (phone): whether the pointer's place says nothing this frame (above): on the app's dock or BAR's
-- interface, past the map's edge, or with fingers a building just picked or a pointer that has not moved since the last
-- test (the building it was picked as, or the twin that test chose, kept)
local droidDef, droidX, droidY
local function droidPointerStale(unitDefID, pos)
	local mx, my = spGetMouseState()
	local picked = unitDefID ~= droidDef
	local moved = mx ~= droidX or my ~= droidY
	droidDef, droidX, droidY = unitDefID, mx, my
	local P = WG.BarDroidPortrait
	local onUi = WG.BarDroidOnInterface
	if (P and P.onDock and P.onDock(mx, my)) or (onUi and onUi(mx, my)) then
		return true
	end
	if pos[1] < 0 or pos[3] < 0 or pos[1] > Game.mapSizeX or pos[3] > Game.mapSizeZ then
		return true
	end
	if WG.BarDroidPadOnly then
		return false
	end
	return picked or not moved
end

-- DrawWorld because update doesn't run pregame
function widget:DrawWorld()
@@@ end

@@@ find
	local unitDefID = isBuilding()
	if not unitDefID then
		return
	end

	local pos = getCursorWorldPosition()
	if not pos then
		return
	end

	local _, _, lmb, _, _ = spGetMouseState()
@@@ with
	local unitDefID = isBuilding()
	if not unitDefID then
		droidDef = nil -- BAR Droid (phone): the next building picked is a new pick, wherever the pointer went meanwhile
		return
	end

	local pos = getCursorWorldPosition()
	if not pos then
		return
	end
	-- BAR Droid (phone): the pointer's place says nothing now (above)
	if droidPointerStale(unitDefID, pos) then
		return
	end

	local _, _, lmb, _, _ = spGetMouseState()
@@@ end
